# Output folder

This plugin writes no file in the project. It does not create `adrenaline/`, `STATUS.md`, or `ORIGIN.json`.

A write to a database, a remote, or a deploy proceeds only when the person wrote the exact phrase in this turn. The phrase is `allow-<class>: <target> — <what>`. One phrase covers one write. A wildcard is not a phrase.

Postgres is a database. INSERT and UPDATE use `allow-db-update`. DELETE, TRUNCATE, DROP, and ALTER use `allow-db-delete`. The target is the database name the person used. There is no `postgres` class.

Do not confirm a read. Do not confirm a local edit, including `git add` and `git commit`.
